## Step by Step Tasks

### 1. Add `generateUniqueFragmentTitle` to `MasRepository`

In `studio/src/mas-repository.js`, add the following method to the `MasRepository` class (e.g., right before `copyFragment`):

```js
/**
 * Returns a unique fragment title by appending a numeric suffix if a fragment
 * with the same title already exists in the current in-memory list.
 * Uniqueness is scoped to the currently-loaded tag path (whatever is in Store.fragments.list.data).
 *
 * Examples:
 *   'lucy-card'   (exists) → 'lucy-card-1'
 *   'lucy-card-1' (exists, 'lucy-card' also exists) → 'lucy-card-2'
 *
 * @param {string} baseTitle - The desired title (typically the title of the fragment being cloned)
 * @returns {string} A title guaranteed not to collide with any title in the in-memory list
 */
generateUniqueFragmentTitle(baseTitle) {
    const existingTitles = new Set(
        (Store.fragments.list.data.get() || [])
            .map((store) => store.get()?.title)
            .filter(Boolean),
    );

    if (!existingTitles.has(baseTitle)) return baseTitle;

    // Strip trailing -N suffix to get the root title
    const suffixMatch = baseTitle.match(/^(.*)-(\d+)$/);
    const rootTitle = suffixMatch ? suffixMatch[1] : baseTitle;

    let n = 1;
    while (existingTitles.has(`${rootTitle}-${n}`)) {
        n += 1;
    }
    return `${rootTitle}-${n}`;
}
```

### 2. Initialize `titleClone` with a unique title in `showClone()`

In `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update `showClone()`:

**Before:**
```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

**After:**
```js
async showClone() {
    if (Store.editor.hasChanges) {
        const confirmed = await this.promptDiscardChanges();
        if (!confirmed) return;
    }
    this.titleClone = this.repository.generateUniqueFragmentTitle(this.fragment.title);
    this.showCloneDialog = true;
    Store.showCloneDialog.set(true);
}
```

### 3. Bind clone dialog title input to `this.titleClone`

In `studio/src/mas-fragment-editor.js`, update the `cloneConfirmationDialog` getter template — change the `sp-textfield` `value` binding:

**Before:**
```js
value="${this.fragment.title}"
```

**After:**
```js
